#!/bin/sh
# Run by Dovecot (conf.d/96-quota.conf) when an account passes 85% or 95% of
# its quota: tells the account, in its own mailbox.
set -eu
percent=$1
user=$2
/usr/sbin/sendmail -f {{ mail_quota_warn_from }} -- "$user" <<MAIL
From: {{ mail_quota_warn_name }} mailserver <{{ mail_quota_warn_from }}>
To: $user
Subject: Uw mailbox is voor $percent% vol / Your mailbox is $percent% full
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Auto-Submitted: auto-generated

De mailbox $user is voor $percent% vol.

Is de mailbox vol, dan kan er geen nieuwe mail meer binnenkomen. Ruim
daarom oude mail op, vooral grote bijlagen, of verplaats mail naar een
archief op uw computer. Leeg daarna de prullenbak.

Meer ruimte nodig? Neem contact op met {{ mail_quota_warn_name }}: {{ mail_quota_warn_from }}.

--

The mailbox $user is $percent% full. When it is full, no new mail can
arrive. Please delete old mail, large attachments especially, and empty
the trash. Need more room? Contact {{ mail_quota_warn_name }}: {{ mail_quota_warn_from }}.
MAIL
